\label{Arbitrary-Result}
Given $T_2>T_1>0$ fixed constants, let $f\in L^2(\Omega)$ and $\tilde{f}\in L^2(0,T;L^2(\Omega))$, and assume that $\beta\in L^{\infty}_{\mu}(\Gamma)$ ($\mu(\cdot)=\mathcal{H}^{N-1}(\cdot)$) is such that $\textrm{ess}\displaystyle\inf_{\Gamma}[\beta]\geq C_{_{\Gamma}}$ for a sufficient large positive constant $C_{_{\Gamma}}$. Then the following hold.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)]\,\,\,Problem (\ref{arbitrary-1.05}) is uniquely solvable over $\mathbb{W}^{\,1}_{\,2}(\overline{\Omega})$.
Moreover, one gets that
$$|\|\mathbf{u}\||_{_{m_1(p),m_2(p)}}\,\leq\,C\left(\|f\|_{_{p,\Omega}}+\|u\|_{_{2,\Omega}}\right),$$
for some constant $C>0$, where
\begin{equation}\label{m1-p}
m_1(p):=\left\{\begin{array}{lcl}
\frac{Np}{N-p},\,\,\textrm{if}\,\,p<N,\\[1ex]
r\in(2^{\ast}_{_N},\infty),\,\,\textrm{if}\,\,p=N,\\[1ex]
\,\,\,\,\,\infty,\,\,\textrm{if}\,\,p>N,
\end{array}
\right.
\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\textrm{and}\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,
m_2(p):=\left\{\begin{array}{lcl}
\frac{(N-1)p}{N-p},\,\,\textrm{if}\,\,p<N;\\[1ex]
s\in(2,\infty),\,\,\textrm{if}\,\,p\geq N,\\[1ex]
\end{array}
\right.
\end{equation}
(for the infinity norm, it is only known in the interior for this case).
\item[(b)]\,\,\,Problem (\ref{arbitrary-1.06}) is uniquely solvable over $C([0,T];L^2(\Omega))\cap L^2((0,T),\mathbb{W}^{\,1}_{\,2}(\overline{\Omega}))$. Moreover,
