\label{equiv-Dirichlet-to-Neumann}
The operator $\mathcal{J}_{_{\Gamma}}$ over $L^2_{\mu}(\Gamma)$ exists, such that the following conditions hold: given $\varphi,\,\psi\in L^2_{\mu}(\Gamma)$,
one has $\varphi\in D(\mathcal{J}_{_{\Gamma}})$ and $\mathcal{J}_{_{\Gamma}}\varphi=\psi$ if and only if there exists $u\in H^1(\Omega)$ satisfying
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)]\,\, $\Delta u=0$;
\item[(b)]\,\, $\varphi$ is the trace of $u$;
\item[(c)]\,\, $\gamma\displaystyle\frac{\partial u}{\partial\nu_{\mu}}\in L^2_{\mu}(\Gamma)$ and
$\gamma\displaystyle\frac{\partial u}{\partial\nu_{\mu}}=\psi$.
\end{enumerate}
